      "local_mate_tree_source": {
        "path": "C:\\Users\\양자\\.codex\\worktrees\\8f44\\Chesstories\\research\\meaning-conditions-20261008\\priced-capture-admission-book-controls.json",
        "sha256": "90b4650114e38c3382055402c133d85e75a348e556dfcd5456c2438d9b966c6e",
        "id": "PC-SG48-SAME-KNIGHT-CAPTURE-FORCING-REPLY"
      },
      "local_tree_legally_rechecked": true,
      "essential_condition": "The forcing queen checks must defeat every current defense at the declared reached check position; the bishop/rook interference and king escape squares determine the result.",
      "events_not_required_identically": "Black may choose Rxf6,Bxf6,exf6,Kf8 or Kg7. The mating route changes; no requirement that Black choose the printed rook capture or a specific final queen capture.",
      "strongest_counter_scope": "At the already reached Nf6 check, every legal Black defense was enumerated and fixed terminal trees replayed. This is a finite conditional mate proof; it does not prove every first Black defense to Rd4 or Rd4 as unique best root move.",
      "counterexample": "Both Rxf6 states have zero immediate legal White recaptures. Before Bg7 leaves, Qh7+ Kf8 Qh8+ Bxh8 is legal; after it leaves, the corresponding Qh8 is mate. Empty recapture inventory cannot mean safe or useful.",
      "basic_comment_allowed": "Rd4 answers mate on b2 and covers c4. If Black takes it with the g7 bishop, Nf6+ interferes with the defenses; even Rxf6 is met by Qh7+ and Qh8 mate.",
      "claim_not_allowed": "No immediate recapture means Rxf6 safely wins the knight; or the conditional mate proves Rd4 is the only winning root choice."
    },
